**Whole task:** a script patches cables, moves knobs and changes them on a schedule. It performs a short piece.

**Our design.** The PAROL6 manual stops at pick-and-place, so this milestone is ours.

## Parts

- The [M5](/lore/m5-touch-the-skiff) and [M6](/lore/m6-patch-a-cable) rig.
- A clock source, chosen with [the skiff](/lore/skiff-target).
- A sequencer script on the PC.

## Concepts

- **Sequencing**, and timing the robot's motion against a musical clock. The arm is slow, so the score is a patch-change score.
- **MIDI and CV control.**
- **Handling failure mid-performance.** A stall means the arm must home again ([Homing](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/05-operation/homing/)).

## How-to

- Our performance scripts.
- The [Python API](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/programming/02-python-api/) program runner.

## Practice

- Rehearsal runs.
- Recovery drills: home again and resume.

## Done check

A 3-minute performance of a written score of patch moves and knob moves on cues, recorded in one take, with Joel narrating what each move does to the sound.

## Terms

- **patch-change score**: a score written as cable and knob moves on cues, slow enough for the arm, instead of a score of notes. Our design.

## Video

[The M7 video](/lore/video-m7) is planned. It is the capstone release: the performance first, then the breakdown.
